Package: horizons
Title: Build and Compare Predictive Models for Mid-Infrared Soil Spectroscopy
Version: 0.9.0
Authors@R: 
    person(given   = "Sam",
           family  = "Leuthold",
           email   = "sam.leuthold@colostate.edu",
           role    = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-4180-7081"))
Description: Builds and compares predictive models from mid-infrared (MIR)
    soil spectra. Reads spectra from Bruker OPUS files or tables, evaluates
    every combination of spectral preprocessing, feature selection, response
    transformation and model type under one cross-validation design, refits
    the best configurations with conformal prediction intervals and an
    applicability-domain check, and stacks them into ensembles. Training sets
    can also be drawn from a reference spectral library. Built on the
    'tidymodels' framework, with parallel execution through 'future'.
